.TH "TTMUX" "1" "July 2026" "TurboTmux" "User Commands"
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
ttmux - TurboTmux session launcher and environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]ttmux\f[R] [\f[B]-v\f[R]|\f[B]--version\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[B]ttmux\f[R] is a simple launcher for \f[B]tmux\f[R](1).
It runs without replacing tmux and does not touch
\f[I]~/.tmux.conf\f[R].
Settings live in \f[I]~/.config/ttmux.conf\f[R].
You can use TurboTmux side by side with ordinary tmux.
.PP
Invoking \f[B]ttmux\f[R] with no arguments attaches to an existing
session named \f[I]ttmux\f[R], or creates one if none exists.
The new session uses a three-pane layout.
No flags or session names are required.
.PP
Out of the box TurboTmux offers a ready three-pane terminal layout,
mouse control, clipboard, and the \f[B]ttbars\f[R](1) plugin for a
status line with a monitor of key resources as pseudographic bars (CPU,
RAM, DISK, ZFS, Btrfs, network ↑ TX / ↓ RX).
.PP
TurboTmux is still almost entirely tmux.
A small set of hotkeys is usually enough (default prefix
\f[B]Ctrl+b\f[R], then the key):
.TP
\f[B]Ctrl+b\f[R],\ \f[B]d\f[R]
Detach from the session.
\f[B]ttmux\f[R] keeps running in the background; the terminal returns to
a normal shell.
.TP
\f[B]Ctrl+b\f[R],\ \f[B]z\f[R]
Zoom the current pane to full screen / restore previous size.
.TP
\f[B]Ctrl+b\f[R],\ \f[B]&\f[R],\ \f[B]y\f[R]
Close the current session (tmux asks for confirmation).
.PP
Optional dependency: \f[B]mc\f[R](1) (launched in the right pane by
default).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]-v\f[R], \f[B]--version\f[R]
Print version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
On first start, if missing, \f[B]ttmux\f[R] creates
\f[I]\[ti]/.config/ttmux.conf\f[R].
It holds basic tmux settings (mouse, clipboard, colors, status line) and
TurboTmux layout parameters.
The file is created once and is not overwritten.
.PP
Layout variables (empty command = interactive shell;
\f[I]ttmux_pane_right_run\f[R] defaults to \f[B]mc\f[R] if installed):
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
ttmux_pane_left_run=\[aq]\[aq]
ttmux_pane_right_run=\[aq]mc\[aq]
ttmux_pane_bottom_run=\[aq]cd /my/project\[aq]
ttmux_pane_right_width_pct=70
ttmux_pane_bottom_height=1
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
If \f[I]\[ti]/.config/mc/\f[R] is missing, \f[B]ttmux\f[R] also creates
an mc config: dark skin and arrow-key navigation.
.PP
The status line includes \f[B]ttbars\f[R] in plugin mode:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
set -g status-left \[aq]#(ttbars -tmux)\[aq]
set -g status-interval 1
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Edit later with a text editor, e.g.\ \f[B]nano\f[R]
\f[I]\[ti]/.config/ttmux.conf\f[R].
.PP
If mouse selection fails on some systems, comment out mouse support in
that file:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
# set -g mouse on
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
ℹ️ manage \f[B]tmux\f[R] panes with hotkeys:
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
lw(30.0n) lw(40.0n).
T{
Keys
T}@T{
Action
T}
_
T{
\f[B]Ctrl+b\f[R], \f[B]↑\f[R]/\f[B]↓\f[R]/\f[B]←\f[R]/\f[B]→\f[R]
T}@T{
switch pane
T}
T{
\f[B]Ctrl+b\f[R],
\f[B]Alt\f[R]+\f[B]↑\f[R]/\f[B]↓\f[R]/\f[B]←\f[R]/\f[B]→\f[R]
T}@T{
resize the current pane
T}
.TE
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[I]\[ti]/.config/ttmux.conf\f[R]
tmux config and layout for TurboTmux.
.TP
\f[I]\[ti]/.config/mc/\f[R]
Also created by \f[B]ttmux\f[R] if missing (dark skin, arrow keys);
never overwritten.
.TP
\f[I]\[ti]/.config/ttbars.conf\f[R]
Personal metrics settings for \f[B]ttbars\f[R](1).
.TP
\f[I]/etc/ttbars.conf\f[R]
System metrics settings for \f[B]ttbars\f[R](1).
